<p class="eyebrow">4.35.0 release review · energy investigation and recipe changes</p>
<h1>Keep energy moving past<br>a <em>nearly full machine.</em></h1>
<p class="standfirst">A machine with just one FE of space left could leave the machines behind it empty—even with a full energy cube. The SFM 4.35.0 candidate keeps the source available when a small extraction fails, so later consumers can still receive power.</p>
<p class="release-scope">This is a combined release review. The <a href="#reproduce">energy deep dive</a> investigates <a href="https://github.com/TeamDman/SuperFactoryManager/issues/610">#610: machines not receiving energy</a>. The <a href="#release-changes">release-wide file explorer</a> also includes separate <a href="#recipe-namespace">recipe-namespace changes</a>, tracked in <a href="https://github.com/TeamDman/SuperFactoryManager/issues/527">#527</a> and reported in <a href="https://github.com/TeamDman/SuperFactoryManager/issues/621">#621</a>. Those recipe changes are not part of the energy-transfer explanation.</p>
<div class="status-line"><span class="candidate">Release candidate · not yet released</span><span>Real-mod runtime evidence: Minecraft 1.21.1</span><span>Packages built for 10 targets</span></div>
