<section id="reproduce">
<div class="reading">
<span class="section-number">01 · Reproducing the stall</span><h2>A full source. An empty consumer.</h2>
<p>Community symptoms and the suspected quantity-sensitive mechanism are tracked in <a href="https://github.com/TeamDman/SuperFactoryManager/issues/610">issue #610</a>. The following is our controlled pinned-mod reproduction.</p>
<p>In the baseline run, the later machine gets no power even though the cube is still full. The full cube and empty later-consumer views show the same controlled second-pass result. Between them, the initial dropper capture records the earlier 25-FE setup before any SFM transfer. They were opened and captured separately after the fixture froze the result; they are not a simultaneous view of both screens.</p>
</div>
<div class="comparison">{{ baseline_pair }}</div>
<div class="reading">
<p>The program is straightforward: take Forge Energy from a Mekanism cube, then supply two destinations in order. The first is an idle Just Dire Things Advanced Dropper. The second is another dropper acting as a consumer that needs power.</p>
