<div class="comparison">{{ fixed_pair }}</div>
<div class="figure-context"><p><strong>How the comparison was controlled.</strong> Between the two passes, the fixture refills the cube and drains the later consumer. It then freezes the program state for capture. This isolates the one-FE obstruction; it is not a continuous natural-gameplay trace.</p><p><strong>What the tooltip can tell us.</strong> The later consumer’s visible <code>0/100.0k FE</code> and <code>100.0k/100.0k FE</code> readings distinguish empty from full. The first dropper’s ordinary tooltip rounds both 99,999 and 100,000 FE to <code>100.0k</code>, so its one-FE gap is established by runtime state, not by extra precision in the pixels.</p></div>
